<title>SWEDEN: Trelleborg in new Mexican prospecting agreement.</title>
<headline>Trelleborg in new Mexican prospecting agreement.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish mining and rubber group Trelleborg said on Friday its mining unit Boliden reached another prospecting agreement in Mexico.</p>
<p>&quot;Partner in the new deal is the Mexican gold and silver producer Luismin and it concerns concessions of 6,000 hectares in a well-known mining district in Durango,&quot; chief executive Kjell Nilsson told the company's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>He did not disclose further details about the agreement.</p>
<p>Boliden has already signed three different cooperation agreements for prospecting abroad this year -- in the Baltic Sea region, in Argentina and in Mexico.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 101</p>
</text>
